# 🎬 Automatic Audio Description for Short Videos

This project presents a lightweight pipeline for generating audio descriptions (AD) for short-form videos, aimed at improving accessibility for visually impaired users.

It focuses on low-resource settings where large-scale commercial solutions may not be feasible.

---

## 🚀 Features

* Scene detection from video
* Frame extraction and visual analysis (VLM)
* Text generation with LLM (context-aware descriptions)
* Subtitle (SRT) generation
* Text-to-speech using Piper
* Audio mixing (original + AD)
* Demo webpage for playback

---

## 🧠 System Overview

**Pipeline:**

Video → Scene Detection → Frame Extraction → Vision-Language Model →
Language Model (summarization) → Subtitles → Text-to-Speech → Audio → Final Video

---

## 🧠 Models Used

* VLM: LLaVA (via Ollama)
* LLM: LLaMA 3.1 (8B)
* TTS: Piper

---

## ⚙️ Installation

Install Python dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Make sure you have Ollama installed and running.

Pull the required models:

```bash
ollama pull llava
ollama pull llama3.1:8b
```

Install ffmpeg (required for audio/video processing):

**macOS:**

```bash
brew install ffmpeg
```

**Linux (Ubuntu/Debian):**

```bash
sudo apt install ffmpeg
```

**Windows:**
Download from: https://ffmpeg.org/download.html
and add it to your system PATH.

---

## ▶️ Usage

Run commands from the project root directory.

### 1. Generate subtitles

```bash
PYTHONPATH=. python scripts/generate_subtitles.py
```

### 2. Generate audio and final video

```bash
PYTHONPATH=. python scripts/generate_media.py
```

---

## 🎥 Demo

A simple demo webpage is included.

Start a local server:

```bash
cd demo
python -m http.server 8000
```

Then open in your browser:

```
http://localhost:8000
```

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
src/        - core pipeline modules
scripts/    - runnable scripts
data/       - input/output files
demo/       - demo webpage
models/     - TTS models
```

---

## 📊 Evaluation

The system can be evaluated based on:

* Clarity
* Usefulness
* Naturalness
* Timing

---

## ⚠️ Limitations

* Visual model may miss details or produce imperfect descriptions
* Descriptions may sometimes be overly simple
* Processing is not real-time

---

## 🔮 Future Work

* Web application for user-uploaded videos
* Multi-audio track support in video players
* Larger-scale evaluation with users

